WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.613
CSIS warned every Prime Minister since 2004.

00:00:03.613 --> 00:00:06.693
Twenty years of documented intelligence briefings.

00:00:06.693 --> 00:00:09.079
Politicians received the intelligence.

00:00:09.079 --> 00:00:11.125
Politicians took minimal action.

00:00:11.125 --> 00:00:16.727
Three undeclared Beijing police stations operated on Canadian soil for diaspora intimidation.

00:00:16.727 --> 00:00:22.102
Eleven ridings identified by CSIS where PRC-linked actors attempted election interference.

00:00:22.102 --> 00:00:27.727
The Hogue Commission confirmed interference in the 2019 and 2021 federal elections.

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:36.090
Hardeep Singh Nijjar — a Canadian citizen and Sikh activist — was assassinated on Canadian soil on June 18th, 2023.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:39.124
The Prime Minister attributed it to Indian government agents.

00:00:39.124 --> 00:00:43.715
The Foreign Influence Transparency Registry became law in June 2024.

00:00:43.715 --> 00:00:47.568
After six hundred and fifty-eight days: zero registrations.

00:00:47.568 --> 00:00:50.999
The mechanism that would force transparency remains dormant.

00:00:50.999 --> 00:00:52.784
Twenty years of warnings.

00:00:52.784 --> 00:00:54.840
Zero meaningful consequences.
